<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τίτῠρος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σάτυρος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				3.40
			</span></i>; 
				Dor.
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1157.39
			</span></i>; Sicilian for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σιληνοί</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σάτυροι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράγοι</span> acc. to Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				3.2
			</span></i> (dub. l.); but <i><span class="en">
				Str.
			</span></i> distinguishes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τίτυροι</span> from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σάτυροι</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σιληνοί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				10.3.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a common
			shepherd's name, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				3.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίτυρος, ὁ</span>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάτυρος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i>, <i>short-tailed ape</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				5.9
			</span></i>, Sch. Theoc.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Lacon.
			 name for <i>the bell-wether</i>, Serv.ad Verg.<i>E.
				Prooem.; he-goat</i>, Sch.Theoc.l.c.; also called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτυρίς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> a kind of bird, also
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτύρας</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τατύρας</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>reed</i> or <i>pipe</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτύρινος</span>), Id.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
